=== plain ===
\e[48;2;52;53;65m\e[0m
\e[48;2;52;53;65m what does the accented file say? 🖊\e[0m
\e[48;2;52;53;65m\e[0m
\e[3m\e[38;2;150;152;150mReading the file with the combining marks in its name.\e[0m\e[0m

The name is written \e[38;2;192;128;80mcafé\e[0m rather than \e[38;2;192;128;80mcafé\e[0m, so the accent is a mark of its own.

A family 👨‍👩‍👧 is one glyph joined from several, and a heart ❤️ asks to be drawn in colour.

Combining marks pile up too: á̂̃̄ is one letter under four of them.

A spacing mark is not a combining one: Thai \e[38;2;192;128;80mกำ\e[0m and Devanagari \e[38;2;192;128;80mकि\e[0m are two characters apiece, and each takes the one cell its base took.

A keycap 1️⃣ asks for two, where a bare 1⃣ keeps the one its digit had.

Word\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0mCells
\e[38;2;192;128;80mกำ\e[0m\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0m1
\e[38;2;192;128;80mकि\e[0m\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0m1
\e[38;2;192;128;80m1️⃣\e[0m\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0m2
\e[38;2;192;128;80m👨‍👩‍👧\e[0m\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0m2
\e[38;2;192;128;80méclair\e[0m\e[38;2;150;152;150m | \e[0m6

A styled wide rune has nowhere to go in one column: \e[38;2;192;128;80m日本\e[0m in code, \e[1m中文\e[0m in bold.

And a result that came back with Windows line endings:
one
two
three

=== printed ===
\e]133;A\e\\\e[48;2;52;53;65m                                                                                                    \e[0m\r
\e[48;2;52;53;65m what does the accented file say? 🖊                                                                 \e[0m\r
\e[48;2;52;53;65m                                                                                                    \e[0m\r
\r
\e[3m\e[38;2;150;152;150mReading the file with the combining marks in its name.\e[0m\e[0m\r
\r
The name is written \e[38;2;192;128;80mcafé\e[0m rather than \e[38;2;192;128;80mcafé\e[0m, so the accent is a mark of its own.\r
